      "message": "@angelaptcheng@gmail.com I see this other issue apart from the issue u r trying to solve. So, lets understand this too -\n\n \u003e May 18 06:05:19 bmc phosphor-cpld-software-update[1104]: Missing property Polarity on path /xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Yosemite5_SCM_2700/Yosemite5_SCM_CPLD, interface xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.LatticeLCMXO3D_9400Firmware.MuxOutputs1\n\nWhy are we seeing this when the polarity is already defined -https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/entity-manager/configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_scm_2700.json?r\u003ddeb2c37a1836aeb93c1b54289ea2e13f77eaad23#295 \n\n\nIn general, the fix i gave you won\u0027t solve the gpio failure issue and the way i see code it continues even if it fails to read the version (which is again a separate issue).\n\nBut for now lets try to get answer to my above questions and restart work on your patch again.",
